    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\nHi,\r\nThe current behavior of the signature help is very annoying. Most of the time cover test I want to read and is very distracting. Having said that I wont get rid of it since can be useful. We could implement something that mimics the behavior of another plugin [nvim-lsp-completion](https://github.com/mfussenegger/nvim-lsp-compl).\r\n\r\nEspected behavior:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/96259932/bc309ab0-fd0d-4cb8-bcc3-dddf45b68140\r\n\r\n",
