        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> I don't think this is a good idea. Mostly because it would lead to signature help to hide and show on every typed parameter, which is a lot of unnecessary flicker.\r\n\r\nThe behavior I'm describing is a little different. The signature help would show only at the beginning of the function call and we could make is showing customizable. I'll try to be more clear (`|` is the cursor):\r\n\r\n```\r\nlocal function sum(a, b)\r\n  return a + b\r\nend\r\n\r\n\r\n    + - - - After typing '(' after a customizable delay\r\n    |       should appear the signature help\r\n    V\r\nsum(|\r\n   \r\n      + - - - - After typing the first non whitespace letter \r\n      |         the signature help should disappear\r\n    +-+-+\r\n    |   |\r\n    V   V\r\nsum(2 , 3)|\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis shouldn't impact normal typing. If you know the function you will type a non whitespace character before triggering the signature help. As I said the current behaviour I think is very distracting and that I consider unnecessary flicker. \r\n\r\nIf you are open to the idea I can adventure with a PR and let you decide after trying it, if you like it or not.",
